// Clue Name :
"P1326590023" "Earpiece"
// DetailString :
"P3920357812" "The Resistance Clockwork gave you a small earpierce. There are some loose wires on certain parts of the device, but it looks like it should work."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - ClockworkKilled 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P1640321987" "Clockwork Retrieved"
// DetailString :
"P483043590" "A few moments after the Clockwork leaves the warehouse, you receive information on your PDA from Reese, saying that they have captured the Clockwork you sent up and are in the process of retrieving information from it.<br><br>Reese reports back shortly afterwards that they were able to discover the location of a Resistance base from that Clockwork. A squad of PPD are now on their way to the hideout."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - ChoseResistance 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P1759356978" "The Resistance"
// DetailString :
"P2926153087" "Despite being sent into the tunnels to arrest a member of the Resistance, you chose to side with them, freeing the man who guided you through the ghoul-infested tunnels."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - ChoseLoyalist 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P574377745" "The Loyalists"
// DetailString :
"P2108565840" "You fulfilled the mission that Reese sent you on, putting down the member of the Resistance you were sent in to find."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - DialogTree 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page NoHeal Text :
"P642927368" "<color slategray>LoA.dIn.G[pRE.rec.MSG] // reLAyinG Me$$^&!</color><br><br>Greetings, {HeroName}. I am a-a-a-a Clockwork programmed t-t-to aid the Resistance. <br><br>The ma-ma-ma-ma-ma-person you are to meet is currently on the r-r-r-run from the PPD. I have been se-se-se-sent to sp-sp-sp...<br><br><color slategray>buF[msg]; nop; mSg=buf // buffERinG meSS^%1</color><br><br>Please use the supply crate to retrieve a-a-a-a-a... some inspirations."
// Answer Text :
"P3936123470" "Alright."
// Answer Text :
"P3031954409" "(Optional) Wait, how do I use the supply crate?"
// Page HowToClickie Text :
"P2556909079" "<color orange>Some missions have an objective to find one or more <color yellow>'glowies'</color> within the map. Glowies glow and give off a humming sound. You activate the glowie by left-clicking it.<br><br>Activate the crate glowie to retrieve your inspirations.</color>"
// Answer Text :
"P931464863" "Ah. Gotcha."
// Page Heal Text :
"P3441658824" "DEPRECATED<color deepskyblue>Welcome to Praetoria</color><br><br>You have co-co-collected an inspiration, now you have to use it in order to heal.<br><br>Inspirations: <color orange>Click on the Inspiration text above your powers tray. This will open a small window where you will see a green health inspiration. Clicking the health inspiration will heal your character.<br><br><span align=center><img src=Tut_P_TrayWInspn.tga></span>"
// Answer Text :
"P3431942317" "Hold on, let me use this inspiration..."
// Answer Text :
"P1800374379" "Okay, I've healed... Now what?"
// Page Heal2 Text :
"P425395864" "DEPRECATED<color deepskyblue>Welcome to Praetoria</color><br><br>You have co-co-collected an inspiration. I would advise w-w-waiting to use that when the time is right - it will increase your damage for a short amount of time.<br><br>Inspirations: <color orange>Click on the Inspiration text above your powers tray. This will open a small window where you will see a red power inspiration. Clicking the power inspiration will increase your character's damage for a short period of time.<br><br><span align=center><img src=Tut_P_TrayWInsp.tga></span>"
// Answer Text :
"P2136981924" "Okay, now what?"
// Answer Text :
"P4060782435" "Leave"
// Page Healed Text :
"P1664588919" "Here, please ta-take this earpiece. The man you are su-supposed to meet with will speak with you through it.<br><br>I have been instructed to give you additional data if required."
// Answer Text :
"P4231960085" "I'm ready to get moving. What's next?"
// Answer Text :
"P4268280258" "(Optional) I'd like a better idea of what's going on here."
// Answer Text :
"P1020541019" "(Optional) Tell me how Inspirations work."
// Page HowToInspirations Text :
"P942443127" "<color orange>Click on the Inspirations text on your powers tray to open your inspirations window. You can right-click inspirations to learn about them, and left-click to activate them.<br><br>You have a Righteous Rage and a Resurgence. Righteous Rage will increase your damage output for 60 seconds, while the Resurgence will heal you a great deal. Inspirations are single-use only. There are several kinds of inspirations.<br><br><span align=center><img src=Tut_P_TrayWInsp.tga></span>"
// Page Door Text :
"P1456149131" "G-good l-l-luck, {HeroName}."
// Page Info Text :
"P419151089" "<color slategray>LoA.dIn.G[rDa.taB.aSe] // enCylopedIA M0!]#</color><br><br>A-a-affirmed. First p-p-programmed s-s-speech a-a-alert launching.<br><br>The Resistance are a g-g-group of f-f-freedom fighters led by Calvin Scott. T-t-their goal is to b-bring down the t-t-yrant, Marcus Cole. H-he has taken away t-too many of o-our l-liberties in the n-name of peace. T-t-the f-f-final straw for the Resistance was the r-r-removal of the freedom of thought. A-a-all t-thoughts of the people of P-praetoria are now m-monitored by th-th-the <color yellow>Seers</color>.<br><br>With Cole's de-destruction, the p-people of P-p-praetoria will be free once more.<br><br>Pl-pl-please tell me what else I can prop-properly inform you on."
// Answer Text :
"P3184447152" "(Optional) Tell me about Emperor Cole."
// Answer Text :
"P2980070641" "(Optional) What does your database say about Praetoria?"
// Answer Text :
"P3924943055" "(Optional) Tell me about the other Clockwork."
// Page Cole Text :
"P113042449" "Em-em-emperor Marcus Cole is the Emperor of the Earth. The hi-hi-history books have recorded that he has saved the world countless times over. It is said he has withstood a nuclear attack and has fended off <color red>Hamidon</color> with his bare hands. The pe-pe-people of Praetoria believe that he is a god come to show us the way to perfection.<br><br>He claims re-re-responsibility for saving Praetoria from the br-brink of total destruction and creating the ut-ut-utopia that it is today."
// Answer Text :
"P2691492907" "I'm ready to go"
// Answer Text :
"P2256304052" "(Optional) How does Cole keep the peace here?"
// Page Praetoria Text :
"P4289869671" "Praetoria is the ca-ca-capital city of Earth. It acts as the seat of power for the rest of the world.<br><br>It is broken up into a se-se-several districts. We're currently below No-no-nova Praetoria, the heart of Praetoria. This is wh-where Emperor Cole's tower is located. You can see the to-to-tower from anywhere in the city. Imperial City is the thriving business area you may have seen across the river before you came down here. Finally, there is Neutropolis which is where all the scientific research and de-de-development are done."
// Answer Text :
"P2550430720" "(Optional) Tell me more about the Resistance."
// Page PPD Text :
"P3630552448" "The Praetorian Police Department or the P.P.D. are Cole's po-po-police force that are given full authority to keep peace in Praetoria. The people are do-do-docile for the most part, so there is not much of a need for them on a da-da-daily basis.<br><br>There are several divisions of the P.P.D., such as the Powers Division, a gro-gr-group of beings with super powers. You were id-id-identified as a member of the Powers Division - ev-ev-every being in Praetoria who has heightened abilities mu-mu-must be registered with the Powers Division. <color deepskyblue>Praetor White</color> is in charge of the Powers Division."
// Page Resistance Text :
"P557350868" "<color slategray>Qry=reS; gEt.tru[haX.dat[rEs]] // feTcH trU!#</color><br><br><color slategray>DAt=chk; oVR.Wrt[dAT[rEs]] // datA OVerrrr!]#</color><br><br>The Re-re-re-resistance are a small group of people who believe that Cole's rule is not what it appears to be. Most Resistance members in Praetoria would be immediately recognized by the monitors topside, so must stay underground to avoid capture.<br><br>The Resistance fights for tho-those who have been run over by Cole's governmental machine, trying to help those who can't help themselves while att-att-attempting to change the government by any means necessary."
// Answer Text :
"P20907075" "(Optional) Tell me about the P.P.D."
// Page Clockwork Text :
"P2209478401" "The Cl-cl-clockwork are Praetoria's work force. We were in-in-invented and designed by<color yellow> Praetor Keys</color>. We do the work that others do not want to-to-to do. We are also used by the P.P.D. to help retrieve anyone they believe is going to be a problem. We ask no questions and do exactly as we're told.<br><br>Some Clockwork, like myself, have been repr-pr-programmed by the Resistance to serve their purposes."
// Page DestroyDoor Text :
"P3194184405" "I ha-ha-have been told to direct you to the do-do-door up ahead. You ca-ca-can destroy it to mo-mo-move forward. I will stay here in the me-me-me-meantime until events on the su-surface have calmed.<br><br><color orange>You now have a choice - you can choose to leave the Clockwork down here, or convince it that the PPD have cleared away from the surface. If the Clockwork goes to the surface, the PPD will scan it for all information regarding the Resistance, then destroy it.<br><br>These choices will appear throughout your travels in Praetoria. They will not change your alignment, however some decisions may bring consequences later on.</color>"
// Answer Text :
"P2385719541" "(Leave)"
// Answer Text :
"P2317688301" "(Convince the Clockwork to go topside)"
// Page DestroyDoorReese Text :
"P585724369" "I ha-ha-have been told to direct you to the do-do-door up ahead. You ca-ca-can destroy it to mo-mo-move forward. I will stay here in the me-me-me-meantime until events on the su-surface have calmed.<br><br><color orange>You now have a choice - you can choose to leave the Clockwork down here, or convince it that the PPD have cleared away from the suface. If the Clockwork goes to the surface, the PPD will scan it for all information regarding the Resistance, then destroy it.<br><br>These choices will appear throughout your travels in Praetoria. They will not change your alignment, however some decisions may bring consequences later on.</color>"
// Answer Text :
"P125736061" "(Optional) (Convince the Clockwork to go topside)"
// Page Topside Text :
"P2295126205" "Understood {HeroName}, I will re-re-return to the surface. Thank you for your assistance."
// Answer Text :
"P3587735805" "Not a problem."
// Page PickedResistance Text :
"P1057880719" "Good to see you're on our side, {HeroName}, you're a real slammer huh? There's someone who wants to speak with you. I think you might've heard of him - <color yellow>Calvin Scott</color>. He's here now, near the entrance back to topside. You should go speak with him - he'll tell you what's gotta be done.<br><br>Good luck."
// Answer Text :
"P2587868253" "I'll go speak with Calvin Scott."
// Page PickedLoyalist Text :
"P1728885369" "You made the right choice, {HeroName}. Calvin Scott and his little band of subversives want only to tear down the utopia Emperor Cole has built for us.<br><br>Just remember, we don't <i>need</i> you here. The PPD has what it takes to bring down the Resistance - without the help from super-powered types like <i>you</i>.<br><br><color yellow>Provost Marchand</color> is coming down to speak with you - looks like he's taken an interest in you."
// Answer Text :
"P2100774194" "(Optional) What's your problem? I just helped you with that Resistance soldier!"
// Page MyProblem Text :
"P965627279" "The <i>problem</i>, {HeroName}, is that I don't like it when someone assumes they can do my job <i>better</i> than me. We all know that Cole is recalling supers from all over the world because he thinks the PPD are slacking off in bringing down the Resistance.<br><br>We're out to show you <i>and</i> Emperor Cole that the PPD have what it takes to stop this Resistance threat - even if we don't have your heightened abilities.<br><br>I'm here to keep my job, even if some other members of the PPD are slacking off. Got it?"
// Answer Text :
"P3755336280" "Easy there. I'd best go speak with the Provost before you say something you'll regret."
// Answer Text :
"P2534721268" "Back off, buddy. I see you've lost several men today, don't let it get to you."
// Answer Text :
"P1441193948" "We fighting the good fight together, officer. Remember that."
// Page ImResistant Text :
"P674587686" "You picked resistance... But I don't know that. However, I still don't trust you."
// Page ImLoyalist Text :
"P2682129929" "You're a Loyalist, which means I should like you. I don't. Deal with it."
// Page Fallback Text :
"P542885946" "What?"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - CalvinScott 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P171665434" "{HeroName}, good to see you. I'm the leader of the Resistance here in Praetoria. I'm pleased to see you're on our side - to be honest, I was a little nervous that you were going to turn on us."
// Answer Text :
"P2840620893" "Let's get to work."
// Answer Text :
"P3588913669" "(Optional) Why are you here talking to me? How did you get here?"
// Page InformationPage1 Text :
"P614336683" "I usually try to be present when we get someone already registered with the <color yellow>Powers Division</color> to come on board. Most of our members who have super-powers are usually renegade - they can't be seen topside.<br><br><i>You</i>, however, are different. The Praetorian government sees you as a loyal follower. I want to use that to our advantage - since you've shown you want to help the Resistance."
// Answer Text :
"P626154003" "I'm ready to get working."
// Answer Text :
"P1375307439" "(Optional) How are we going to use that?"
// Page InformationPage2 Text :
"P1414694154" "I'm not too sure how gung-ho you were with the Powers Divison before, but now we need you to be all for it.<br><br>If you're going to do work for the Resistance, we're going to need Cole and his goons to believe you're on their side.<br><br>To that end, <color yellow>I need you to speak with Praetor White and work your way deeper into the Powers Division.</color>"
// Answer Text :
"P1161262865" "(Optional) So, I'm still to do the work of the Loyalists?"
// Page Loyalists Text :
"P2784806764" "Not exactly.<br><br>Once you've proven to Praetor White that you're a 'fine, upstanding member of the Powers Division', you can seek out members of the Resistance throughout Praetoria - maybe even normal folk who are sympathetic to our cause.<br><br><i>Then</i> you'll be able to fight the good fight. Just remember though, <i>you need to keep up the facade that you're with the Powers Division.</i> It's difficult, but we need a {Hero.gender=male man|woman} within the organization.<br><br>There is... another way you could help us, if you're interested in hearing me out."
// Answer Text :
"P3780741117" "I'll figure it out as I go - I'm going topside."
// Answer Text :
"P1769938361" "(Optional) What's the other way?"
// Page OtherWay Text :
"P3893502903" "We have plenty of people fighting the good fight, but only a few... insiders within the Loyalists.<br><br>We could use someone who works exclusively with the Loyalists. It'll be a dangerous job - and you'll have to be sure not to get caught. You'll probably have to do some... questionable things against us in order to gain the full trust of the Loyalists as well.<br><br>However, when you get to major operations, you can contact me. We'll figure out what you can do to turn the operation towards our favor.<br><br><color orange>You have the option, as a member of the Resistance, to do missions on the sides of the Loyalists. They will play through normally, however at certain points you will be able to contact Calvin Scott to add options to the mission in order to swing events in favor of the Resistance.</color>"
// Answer Text :
"P3393345752" "I'll think on it. For now, I'm going topside."
// Page Conclusion Text :
"P3775242503" "Good luck then, {HeroName}. You'll want to contact Praetor White as soon as you get topside. Be careful around Praetor White. He's brutal, cruel, and selfish. Show any weakness around him and he'll break you in half. You might not like it, but for now you'll have to put up with his attitude.<br><br>And remember, we need you as our inside {Hero.gender=Male man|girl} in Powers Division. Do what you need to do to gain their trust, but don't believe <i>anything</i> those Loyalist scum tell you."
// Answer Text :
"P1544711594" "I'll make sure to be careful."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - Marchand 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P3390137552" "Hello, {HeroName}. I am <color yellow>Provost Marshal Gerard T. Marchand</color>. I run all military operations for Emperor Cole - this means I also help run the PPD. <br><br>I'm impressed at your actions here today with the Resistance. Look around you, {HeroName}. All of these PPD died trying to get this one Resistance member. It's inefficient. I've done my best with the PPD, but it isn't enough.<br><br>We need people like <i>you</i> to help defend Praetoria against the Resistance, and other threats. <br><br>And believe me, there are <i>many</i> that would seek to destroy our beautiful city."
// Answer Text :
"P2860215001" "Right, look, let's just get moving. What's the next step?"
// Answer Text :
"P1123669436" "(Optional) What are these other threats?"
// Page Threats Text :
"P323198096" "Currently in Nova Praetoria we're dealing with the <color yellow>Destroyers</color>, a group of psychopaths who, as you may guess, wish to spread destruction amongst our beautiful city.<br><br>They are our top priority on the surface of Praetoria, next to the Resistance. We, of course, always have the threat of <color yellow>Hamidon</color> lurking outside of Nova, but our sonic barriers are keeping the beast at bay."
// Answer Text :
"P2723433343" "Okay, what's next?"
// Answer Text :
"P2362537516" "(Optional) Wait, what's a Hamidon?"
// Page Hamidon Text :
"P3206199008" "You don't know?<br><br>Hamidon is a monster of pure malice. It nearly destroyed the <i>entire</i> world during the <color yellow>Hamidon Wars</color> in the 70's.<br><br>Emperor Cole is the only reason why we still exist today. He rallied the people of this land to fight the monsters of Hamidon and eventually faced off against the beast by himself.<br><br>Though Cole did not destroy Hamidon, he was able to push the monster back, allowing us the chance to rebuild civilization.<br><br>We're safe from Hamidon, for now, though it is a threat that still looms over us."
// Answer Text :
"P3003218789" "Interesting. So, what's next?"
// Page NextStep Text :
"P162922511" "<color yellow>You'll need to exit through the door behind me to speak with Praetor White.</color><br><br>While I am in charge of Praetoria's military, he is the head of Powers Division. You'll be able to start your career in protecting Praetoria - or perhaps your rise to power - with him.<br><br>He is somewhat rough around the edges, but I fully trust him with the safety of our great city."
// Answer Text :
"P1139723102" "Sounds good."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - Marauder 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page ChoseLoyalist Text :
"P4120437140" "<color orange>Praetor White looks at you beneath his glasses, cracking his neck.</color><br><br>{HeroName}, heard a lot of things about you. Don't go getting all cocky just 'cause you took down some member of the Resistance. You're talkin' to the guy who fought durin' the <color yellow>Hamidon Wars</color>, so I ain't impressed hearin' that someone took down a stupid idealist who could use a gun.<br><br>But you got my attention, so that means something - for now.<br><br>You got some spark in you, even if you're still on the same level as most of the super-powered dogs here in Praetoria. Me? I'm the Top Dog, I keep all the other powered dogs in line.<br><br>You wanna get noticed, you break yourself away from the pack and join mine. That what you're trying to do, {HeroName}? "
// Answer Text :
"P1359950983" "That's the idea, Praetor White."
// Page InformationPage1 Text :
"P3653934899" "I see a lotta ambition in you, {HeroName}, but that ain't just give you a free pass into my group. <br><br>If you really wanna get through the Powers Division though, we're gonna have to make sure you've got the skills it takes to stand side by side with us. You think you've got what it takes? 'Cause I ain't got time to babysit any dogs when I could just throw you away."
// Answer Text :
"P4016204973" "I can handle whatever is thrown at me."
// Answer Text :
"P2033417013" "I've got what it takes, believe me. What's next?"
// Answer Text :
"P3956344654" "I delivered that Clockwork to you, didn't I?"
// Page InformationPage1Reese Text :
"P1571712547" "Tough talk now that you're with me, {HeroName}. Seems like you changed your tune from just a while ago. Reese told me how you were wantin' out of the Powers Division.<br><br>Seems funny that you're suddenly all gung-ho about it. Maybe you got wise, or maybe you got a trick up your sleeve.<br><br>All I know is that I'm gonna be keepin' my eye on you. You got some potential, talkin' to Reese like that, but we'll have to see if you've got what it takes to hold your own within <i>my</i> group in the Powers Division."
// Answer Text :
"P2742403230" "Alright, what's next?"
// Answer Text :
"P2641818225" "I delivered that Clockwork to you. I think that goes to show my potential - and my loyalty."
// Page InformationPage2 Text :
"P1842453176" "Hah! That's the spirit. Before we get underway, {HeroName}, there's something you should know.<br><br>There's a lot of stuff to be done here in Praetoria - keeping the peace and what not.<br><br>Once you prove yourself as a member of the Powers Division, you can either continue during work with the Loyalists, or you can go undercover into a Resistance cell. You'll have to do a lotta things for those scum in the Resistance, but it'll help us get some inside dirt on them - like wherever their main hub is.<br><br><color orange>You have the option, as a member of the Loyalists, to do missions on the sides of the Resistance. They will play through normally, however at certain points you will be able to contact a high-ranking official in the Loyalist to add options to the mission to swing events in favor of the Loyalist.</color>"
// Page ClockworkDelivered Text :
"P441180038" "That was you huh? Reese told me he was the one who tracked down that piece of tin.<br><br>Yeah, you did good on that. We found out the location of one of their bases with that piece of Clockwork. Looks like those punks have been snatching Clockwork from right under our noses to use for themselves! Maybe this little encounter will teach 'em to keep their grubby paws to themselves, at least 'till I get a hold of them to cut 'em off!"
// Answer Text :
"P323297320" "So what's the first step in all of this?"
// Page FirstStep Text :
"P1972475409" "Well, before we get underway, {HeroName}, there's something you should know.<br><br>There's a lot of stuff to be done here in Praetoria - keeping the peace and what not.<br><br>Even more though...we need to really strike at the heart of the Resistance. You finding that Clockwork for us, it helped, but those guys are like cockroaches. They're crawling all over the place and making things harder for us.<br><br>Once you prove yourself as a member of the Powers Division, you can either continue during work with the Loyalists, or you can go undercover into a Resistance cell. You'll have to do a lot of ugly things for those scum in the Resistance, but it'll help us get some inside dirt on them - like wherever their main hub is.<br><br><color orange>You have the option as a member of the Loyalists to do missions on the sides of the Resistance. They will play through normally, however at certain points you will be able to contact a high-ranking official in the Loyalist to add options to the mission to swing events in favor of the Loyalist.</color>"
// Page InformationPage3 Text :
"P1131999444" "Next huh?<br><br>We start working, that's what's next!<br><br>Get yourself used to being in the high society of the Loyalists, then come to me and we can get moving towards keeping the peace here in Praetoria.<br><br><color yellow>If you haven't already done so, speak with Praetor Duncan to level up and gain a new power!</color>"
// Answer Text :
"P2868661889" "Will do."
// Page ChoseResistance Text :
"P985742461" "{HeroName}, you think you're all that? You come walking up to me after botching that operation with Wrencher?<br><br>Now <i>I</i> have to explain to the families of those PPD that were down there why their husbands ain't coming back! You think I like trying to act all mopey to those punks?<br><br>You got a lotta work ahead of you if you're gonna get anywhere in the Powers Division. Tell me why I should bother putting you to the test to get to the next level!"
// Answer Text :
"P4099243237" "The operation was all over the place, I can do better with the next one."
// Answer Text :
"P4159134907" "I delivered that Clockwork to you, didn't I? That should prove something."
// Page NextOne Text :
"P644714577" "You're lucky I got an image to maintain, or I'd brawl you right here! Maybe you're right though, maybe you got some spunk to you, enough that you ain't running away with your tail between your legs with me yellin' at you.<br><br>Alright, {HeroName}. You got yourself a second chance to get into my little circle. But, you fail again, and you ain't just gonna be out to do whatever you want - you're gonna pay a visit to them other members of the Powers Division that are on 'vacation', if you catch my drift."
// Answer Text :
"P1707187524" "Drift caught, Praetor White."
// Page ClockworkDelivered2 Text :
"P368053352" "Yeah, you did get us that Clockwork, I'll give you that. Didn't think the Resistance were able to hack into our machines like that yet.<br><br>We got Reese leading a team now to one of them Resistance cells in the tunnels - that Clockwork had a bunch of data within that we were able to use.<br><br><i>Maybe</i> you got what it takes, {HeroName}. Maybe that operation being botched was cause those PPD weren't tough enough. We'll see.<br><br>For now, you got yourself that second chance. Report back to me when you're ready, cause your life is gonna change once you start working under me."
// Answer Text :
"P2786969114" "Will do, Praetor White."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - Rothstein 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page NotNow Text :
"P690287643" "Not now, {HeroName}, we've got ghouls!  {Hero.gender=male Throw in some muscle, soldier|Take down some chompers, missy}!"
// Answer Text :
"P2588408948" "Right!"
// Page Intro2 Text :
"P4240500004" "Whew, man, just our luck huh?<br><br>PPD chase us right into an old ghoul den! Sure hope that Wrencher is doing OK...<br><br>Anyway, the name's <color yellow>Rothstein</color>. You're that new {Hero.gender=male guy|gal} that we're getting from Powers Division, right? Good to have you on board to help us.<br><br><color orange>Despite talking face to face with a high-ranking member of the Resistance, you won't be able to bring him back to the Loyalists, given the sheer amount of support he has around him."
// Answer Text :
"P637445866" "Thanks!"
// Answer Text :
"P3498082413" "(Optional) Tell me more about the Resistance"
// Answer Text :
"P1721097898" "(Optional) What were those things? -Ghouls-?"
// Page Resistance Text :
"P2431715574" "I'll talk to you in <color yellow>plain talk</color> for now, don't wanna get you all confused.<br><br>Us, the Resistance? We're the last, best hope for humanity here in Praetoria. Cole's got all these people brain-washed into thinking that what he decides is best for everyone. But really, it's all just what's best for <i>him</i>.<br><br>Did you know folks can't own their own <i>guns</i> in Praetoria without having to sign up to join the PPD or Powers Division? It's nuts! Cole claims it's because, 'you don't need guns for your own protection when we're protecting you'.<br><br>Us in the Resistance, we're all about <color yellow>power to the people</color> and givin' it to them no matter what.<br><br>You wanna know about them ghouls too, or you goin' forward?"
// Answer Text :
"P2565996097" "Good to know. I need to get moving, though. See you around."
// Answer Text :
"P3420388632" "(Optional) What were those monsters? Ghouls?"
// Page Ghouls Text :
"P3192354213" "I'll talk to you in <color yellow>plain talk</color> for now, don't wanna get you all confused.<br><br>Yeah, we ain't really sure what they are. Some of the older guys in the Resistance say that they just sort appeared one day in the tunnels. Ever since then, we gotta be careful of where we go. You get ambushed by a horde of those things, you ain't coming back.<br><br>Those ghouls will <i>eat you alive</i> if they get the chance - they're nothing but a bunch of monsters. Some folks say that <i>we</i> made them, but seriously, what're we gonna use to make those monsters? I <i>wish</i> we could make ourselves an army of monsters to throw at Cole, believe me!<br><br>So you wanna know more about us, or you gotta be headin' forward?"
// Answer Text :
"P3741046858" "Right...well, I need to get going now."
// Page Ghouls2 Text :
"P2472627227" "Yeah, we ain't really sure what they are. Some of the older guys in the Resistance say that they just sort appeared one day in the tunnels. Ever since then, we gotta be careful of where we go. You get ambushed by a horde of those things, you ain't coming back.<br><br>Those ghouls will <i>eat you alive</i> if they get the chance - they're nothing but a bunch of monsters. Some folks say that <i>we</i> made them, but seriously, what're we gonna use to make those monsters? I <i>wish</i> we could make ourselves an army of monsters to throw at Cole, believe me!<br><br>You know somethin', nobody here really stops to smell the roses, y'know? I got a little somethin' for ya, {HeroName}."
// Answer Text :
"P2432280157" "No thanks, I'm good."
// Answer Text :
"P3985354570" "(Optional) What is it?"
// Page Resistance2 Text :
"P112545392" "Us, the Resistance? We're the last, best hope for humanity here in Praetoria. Cole's got all these people brain-washed into thinking that what he decides is best for everyone. But really, it's all just what's best for <i>him</i>.<br><br>Did you know folks can't own their own <i>guns</i> in Praetoria without having to sign up to join the PPD or Powers Division? It's nuts! Cole claims it's because, 'you don't need guns for your own protection when we're protecting you'.<br><br>Us in the Resistance, we're all about <color yellow>power to the people</color> and givin' it to them no matter what.<br><br>You know somethin', nobody here really stops to smell the roses, y'know? I got a little somethin' for ya, {HeroName}."
// Page BADGE Text :
"P8192703" "Here, little token of appreciation, from me to you. Take it easy.<br><br><color yellow>You just received a badge! Badges are awarded for various accomplishments. Some are easier to get than others. To see what badges you have, click on the word 'Badge' located on your navigation bar.</color>"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P868899244" "I need you to infiltrate the Resistance.<br><br>There are Destroyers all over the streets, it's a mess.  Don't be fooled, however.  They're just a set up to distract us from the real threat to peace in Praetoria: <color deepskyblue>the Resistance.</color><br><br>The Resistance is always looking for new recruits. I've made it known that you aren't happy being inducted into Powers Division. This should be enough to get your foot in the door. The rest is on you."
// AcceptString :
"P960773499" "Where should I go to find the recruiter?"
// SendOffString :
"P1443183670" "There's a Resistance recruiter that is ready to meet you.  Go to the door under the nearby underpass; that door will take you into the underground.<br><br>There are worse things than Resistance there, so keep your eyes open.<br><br>Once you make contact with the Resistance member, I will send in additional troops to arrest him and his buddies."
// ActiveTaskString :
"P2475075386" "Locate the Resistance Officer"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P1431132670" "You need to enter the underground, I will send in backup once you make contact.<br><br><color orange>Follow the marker on your compass to the underground entrance.  If the marker gets deselected, you can reselect it by clicking on the mission tab, then selecting the mission from Reese."
// TaskTitle :
"P358628867" "<color deepskyblue>Welcome to Praetoria</color>"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// EntryString :
"P3988328511" "You've made your way into the den where the Resistance are. Up ahead, you can hear the sound of a Clockwork repairing itself."

